  Built with mite: a small static site generator that renders mdoc(7)
  manual pages to HTML with mandoc and glues them together with a
  POSIX Makefile.  No node, no ruby, no bundler, no configuration
  language.

      mite .... https://git.sr.ht/~shrub900/mite
      mandoc .. https://mandoc.bsd.lv/


REQUIREMENTS

    mandoc      renders every .1 source to HTML
    make        drives the build (GNU or BSD make)
    python3     only for `make serve` (local preview)

  Arch Linux
      $ sudo pacman -S mandoc make python

  Debian / Ubuntu
      $ sudo apt-get install mandoc make python3


BUILD

  SITE defaults to fauzymadani.github.io, so plain `make` is enough:

      $ make
      $ make SITE=fauzymadani.github.io

  The whole site is written to out/<site>/, which is disposable:

      $ make clean                  # rm -rf out/<site>

  Nothing outside out/ is generated, so the repository only ever
  holds sources.


PREVIEW

      $ make serve                  # build, then http://127.0.0.1:8000/
      $ make serve PORT=8080

  `make serve` builds first, then serves out/<site>/ with
  python3 -m http.server.  Stop it with Ctrl-C.


REPOSITORY LAYOUT

    bin/helper                   the mite helper (raw/body/sidebar/page/serve)
    Makefile                     build rules
    README.txt                   this file
    pub/style.css                layout + sidebar stylesheet
    pub/mandoc.css               upstream mandoc stylesheet
    sites/<site>/manifest.mk     site config: title, subtitle, dirs, targets
    sites/<site>/mk/*.mk         per-page metadata (drives build + sidebar)
    sites/<site>/<dir>/<page>.1  the actual content, as mdoc(7)
    sites/<site>/_mite/          optional overrides: header.html, footer.html,
                                 style.css, mandoc.css
    out/<site>/                  build output (git-ignored)


ADDING A PAGE

  A page needs two files: an mdoc source and a metadata block.

  1. Write the content, e.g. sites/<site>/words/my-post.1:

        .Dd Nov 7, 2026
        .Dt MY-POST 1
        .Os fauzymadani.github.io
        .Sh NAME
        .Nm my-post
        .Nd one line summary
        .Sh DESCRIPTION
        Body text goes here.
        .Pp
        Second paragraph.

  2. Declare it in the matching mk file, e.g. sites/<site>/mk/words.mk:

        PAGE := words/my-post
        HTML_TARGETS := $(HTML_TARGETS) $(OUT_DIR)/$(PAGE).html

        TITLE.$(PAGE) = my-post
        OS.$(PAGE) = fauzymadani.github.io
        URL.$(PAGE) := /$(PAGE).html

        $(OUT_DIR)/words/my-post.html: $(SRC_DIR)/mk/words.mk
        $(OUT_DIR)/words/my-post.raw.html: $(SRC_DIR)/words/my-post.1

     PAGE is the path under out/ without the extension, TITLE.$(PAGE)
     is the <title> and sidebar label, URL.$(PAGE) is the link target.

  3. Run `make` and check the sidebar.  The nav tree is generated from
     mk/*.mk, not from the filesystem, so a source without a PAGE
     block builds nothing.

  The index and 404 pages are deliberately hidden from the sidebar
  (bin/helper, `sidebar` command).


MDOC MACROS

    .Sh NAME                            section header
    .Nm name                            program/thing name
    .Nd text                            one line description
    .Pp                                 paragraph break
    .Bl -bullet -compact / .It          bullet list
    .Bl -tag -width "X" / .It Foo       tag list (Foo in left column)
    .Bd -literal -offset indent / .Ed   literal / preformatted block
    .Lk url "text"                      hyperlink


STYLING

  pub/style.css
      Page layout, sidebar tree, responsive rules.  Typography is the
      first block: --font-prose (Times New Roman for prose) and
      --font-mono (literal blocks, code, diagrams).  pre is pinned to
      --font-mono on purpose: mandoc.css sets `pre { font-family:
      inherit }`, so ASCII art and unit files would lose their column
      alignment if they inherited a proportional font.  This file is
      linked after mandoc.css, so the overrides survive upstream
      updates.

  pub/mandoc.css
      Upstream mandoc stylesheet.  Colours come from --bg/--fg;
      pub/style.css pins it to dark mode and redefines those two
      variables (#1E1F21 / #C5C8C6).  Near-white body text is too
      harsh against Times New Roman, so the foreground is a muted grey
      and the links are the desaturated #81A2BE / #B294BB.  The page is
      dark regardless of the OS setting (`color-scheme: dark`, <meta
      name="color-scheme">); drop the :root block to follow
      prefers-color-scheme again.

  sites/<site>/_mite/
      Per-site overrides.  style.css there is appended to
      pub/style.css; header.html replaces the default document head
      (it uses @TITLE@, href="/mandoc.css" and href="/pub/style.css"
      placeholders, which mite rewrites with a ?site= cache buster);
      footer.html replaces the default closing tags.


DEPLOY

  .github/workflows/deploy.yml builds on every push to main and
  publishes out/fauzymadani.github.io to GitHub Pages.

  One-time setup in the repository:

      Settings -> Pages -> Build and deployment source = GitHub Actions

  .github/workflows/quality.yml runs the same build on pull requests
  and fails if a source has no output or a page is missing from the
  sidebar.
